WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.212
Five hundred miles an hour.

2
00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:03.849
That is how fast a tsunami can

3
00:00:03.849 --> 00:00:05.591
race across the deep ocean,

4
00:00:05.591 --> 00:00:07.516
as fast as a jet plane.

5
00:00:07.916 --> 00:00:10.261
It begins when an earthquake or a

6
00:00:10.261 --> 00:00:14.685
volcano makes the sea floor move suddenly.

7
00:00:14.685 --> 00:00:16.693
The whole column of water above it

8
00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:19.362
is pushed, and waves spread out.

9
00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:21.155
Out in deep water,

10
00:00:21.155 --> 00:00:22.897
the waves are very long but very

11
00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:23.942
low.

12
00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:26.159
A ship may rise only a metre

13
00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.423
or two, so slowly that the crew

14
00:00:28.423 --> 00:00:29.907
hardly notices.

15
00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:32.408
Near the coast the water gets shallow.

16
00:00:32.408 --> 00:00:33.430
The wave slows,

17
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.009
its length shrinks,

18
00:00:35.009 --> 00:00:36.333
and its height grows,

19
00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:38.409
sometimes into a wall of water.

20
00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:40.771
That is why a tsunami does little

21
00:00:40.771 --> 00:00:42.396
harm out at sea,

22
00:00:42.396 --> 00:00:43.732
and so much at the shore,

23
00:00:43.732 --> 00:00:45.518
where people live and work.

24
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:48.193
After the Indian Ocean tsunami of December

25
00:00:48.193 --> 00:00:49.481
two thousand four,

26
00:00:49.481 --> 00:00:52.268
India joined the international warning system.

27
00:00:52.268 --> 00:00:54.961
Its warnings now come from INCOIS in

28
00:00:54.961 --> 00:00:56.202
Hyderabad.

29
00:00:56.602 --> 00:00:58.773
For GS One and disaster management:

30
00:00:58.773 --> 00:01:01.362
deep water means fast and low.

31
00:01:01.362 --> 00:01:04.100
Shallow water means slow and high.

